@page "/"
@using TelerikSvgIcons4

<PageTitle>Home</PageTitle>

<h1>Legacy v4 Telerik Icons</h1>

This sample app shows how to use v4 Telerik icons with a Telerik UI for Blazor version that depends on v5 icons.

<ul>
    <li><strong>Telerik UI for Blazor</strong> version: @(typeof(TelerikRootComponent).Assembly.GetName().Version)</li>
    <li><strong>Telerik.SvgIcons</strong> version: @(typeof(ISvgIcon).Assembly.GetName().Version)</li>
    <li><strong>TelerikSvgIcons4</strong> version: @(typeof(TelerikSvgIcons4.SvgIcon4).Assembly.GetName().Version)</li>
</ul>

<h2>Using v4 Icons via TelerikSvgIconsV4Service</h2>

<TelerikButton Icon="@SvgIcon.Bold" />
<TelerikButton Icon="@SvgIcon.Italic" />
<TelerikButton Icon="@SvgIcon.Underline" />
<TelerikButton Icon="@SvgIcon.Image" />

<TelerikEditor @bind-Value="@EditorValue"
               Height="120px" />

<h2>Using v5 Icons</h2>

<p>To render built-in v5 Telerik SVG icons while <strong>TelerikSvgIconsV4Service</strong> is active, use the <strong>TelerikSvgIcon</strong> component.</p>

<TelerikSvgIcon Icon="@SvgIcon.Bold" />

<TelerikSvgIcon Icon="@SvgIcon.Italic" />

<TelerikSvgIcon Icon="@SvgIcon.Underline" />

<TelerikSvgIcon Icon="@SvgIcon.Image" />

<h2>Using v4 Icons</h2>

<p><strong>TelerikSvgIconsV4Service</strong> does not run for standalone SVG icons. Set a legacy icon reference directly to display it.</p>

<TelerikSvgIcon Icon="@SvgIcon4.Bold" />

<TelerikSvgIcon Icon="@SvgIcon4.Italic" />

<TelerikSvgIcon Icon="@SvgIcon4.Underline" />

<TelerikSvgIcon Icon="@SvgIcon4.Image" />

@code {
    private string EditorValue { get; set; } = "<p>Telerik Editor for Blazor<p>";
}